# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Values starting VITE_ are built into the app and are public by design:
# anyone can read them from the deployed site. For a deployment, set them
# in your host's build settings (on GitHub: repository Settings > Secrets
# and variables > Actions > Variables), not in a file in the repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app. See docs/google-cloud-setup.md for where each value comes from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. OAuth 2.0 client ID (type "Web application").
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# Required for per-file access (the default). API key restricted to the
# Google Picker API and to your site.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-api-key
# Required for per-file access. The Cloud project NUMBER (not its ID).
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=123456789012

# Optional. Which Google permission the app asks for to store campaigns.
#   file (default)  Per-file access. The app reaches only sheets it created
#                   or that a person chose once in Google's file chooser.
#   sheets          Google Sheets access. Campaigns open straight from a
#                   link and only the client ID is needed, but Google words
#                   it as all the person's spreadsheets and reviews it.
# VITE_GOOGLE_ACCESS=sheets

# Optional. Where people report problems, normally the repository's
# issues page. Linked from the About, Privacy, Terms and FAQ pages.
# VITE_CONTACT_URL=https://github.com/your-name/your-repo/issues
# Optional. The source repository. Linked from the FAQ page.
# VITE_REPO_URL=https://github.com/your-name/your-repo

# Optional. Path the built app is served from. Default "/".
# For a GitHub Pages project site without a custom domain use the
# repository name, e.g. /your-repo/
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev server (vite.config.ts). All optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEV_PORT=8471
# Public hostname of the dev machine. When set, the dev server listens on
# every interface and accepts only this hostname.
# DEV_HOST=dev.example.com
# Certificate and key files. When both are set, the dev server uses HTTPS.
# DEV_TLS_CERT=/path/to/dev.example.com.crt
# DEV_TLS_KEY=/path/to/dev.example.com.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests only. Not needed to run or build the app, and never read by it.
# Used by tests/e2e, tests/integration and scripts/*.mjs.
# The client secret and refresh tokens here ARE secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client secret of the OAuth client the tests use. The tests turn the
# refresh tokens below into access tokens with it.
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
# Two Google test accounts: one runs the campaign, one joins it.
# E2E_GM_EMAIL=gm-test-account@example.com
# E2E_PLAYER_EMAIL=player-test-account@example.com
# Written by: node scripts/capture-refresh-tokens.mjs
# GOOGLE_GM_REFRESH_TOKEN=refresh-token-for-the-gm-account
# GOOGLE_PLAYER_REFRESH_TOKEN=refresh-token-for-the-player-account
# ID of a spreadsheet owned by the GM test account and shared (Editor)
# with the player test account. The tests wipe it on every run.
# SHEETS_FIXTURE_ID=your-test-spreadsheet-id
# Where the E2E tests find the app. Default http://localhost:8471
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8471
# Where scripts/capture-refresh-tokens.mjs listens for Google's redirect.
# CAPTURE_HOST=localhost
# CAPTURE_PORT=9997
# Set to 1 on the command line to run the live Sheets integration test:
#   LIVE_SHEETS=1 npx vitest run tests/integration/sheets-live.test.ts
# LIVE_SHEETS=1
